Subject: [PATCH] sycl: IQ4_NL in the reorder layout, dense and per MoE expert

Local gap fill. IQ4_NL had no reorder (SoA) layout, so its MMVQ read the block layout while Q4_0,
whose block is identical, reads the faster [qs][d] layout. IQ4_NL now takes that layout:

- 2D weights through reorder_qw_planar, MoE experts per slice through reorder_qw_planar_moe, one
  shared tail writer. Slices that are not 16-byte aligned stay in the block layout.
- MMVQ: reorder_vec_dot_q_sycl<IQ4_NL>, Q4_0's lane split with the nibbles mapped through
  kvalues_iq4nl, for 1..8 columns (the IQ3 reorder launchers, widened to the type) and the MoE
  reorder MMVQ.
- The other readers of a reordered weight: the f16 / f32 dequantize of the GEMM route, GET_ROWS (a
  tied embedding is also a MUL_MAT weight), and a SoA stage of the fused / grouped XMX dequant GEMM
  so prompt batches keep that GEMM. Candidate C20's ESIMD MoE GEMM already reads this layout.

The new lines stay off candidate C10's context (its IQ4_XS reorder edits the same lists), so every
candidate still applies with plain git apply.

test-backend-ops: IQ4_NL joins the type lists of test_get_rows_after_mul_mat and
test_mul_mat_reorder_then_big_batch, which check the readers of a weight the reorder was installed on.

